  "final_message": "You're right. The data covers 2023\u20132024, and the only real second-quarter dip is in **2024**. Q2 2023 was about flat with Q1. Almost all of the 2024 dip comes from three ports: **Brackwater, Fennick and Ivelholm**.\n\n**Overall, Q2 2024 was well below the other 2024 quarters:**\n\n| | Q1 | **Q2** | Q3 | Q4 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Shipments | 156 | **115** | 157 | 149 |\n| TEU | 12,991 | **9,622** | 13,290 | 12,029 |\n\nThat's about 3,150 TEU (\u221225%) below the average of the other three quarters.\n\n**Three ports went almost silent in Q2 2024 (TEU):**\n\n| Port | Q1 | **Q2** | Q3 | Q4 | Shipments Q1\u2192Q2 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Brackwater | 1,790 | **466** | 1,839 | 1,463 | 22 \u2192 7 |\n| Fennick | 1,523 | **366** | 2,289 | 1,445 | 19 \u2192 4 |\n| Ivelholm | 2,214 | **375** | 1,507 | 1,630 | 20 \u2192 4 |\n\n- Compared with their usual levels, these three are down about 4,000 TEU combined. That's more than the whole overall drop.\n- The other seven ports together were slightly *up* in Q2 (8,415 TEU, against 7,464 in Q1 and 7,655 in Q3). Without these three ports there is no dip.\n- The low period runs exactly from April through June. The three ports fell from about 60 shipments a month to 5 in each of April, May and June, then bounced straight back in July. That pattern looks like one event, such as a closure, a strike or a data-feed gap, not a gradual slowdown.\n- It isn't tied to one carrier type: container, bulk and tanker shipments all dropped at those ports.\n\nA few smaller things move around too. Glassford has been drifting lower since early 2023, and Dovesend and Juniper Reach were actually up in Q2 2024. None of them is big enough to matter here.\n\nBefore treating this as a real slowdown, it's worth checking whether those three ports' records for April\u2013June 2024 are actually missing. A clean three-month gap with an instant recovery is often a data problem.\n\nI ran this as standalone polars queries and haven't changed `notebooks/explore.py`. I can add these breakdowns to it as cells, maybe with a chart of monthly TEU by port.",
